Description: Start an activatable application itself when it runs on another GPU
 D-Bus activation starts an application with the session bus's environment,
 so the variables of its GPU never reached a DBusActivatable entry: neither
 KDE's own PrefersNonDefaultGPU nor the Graphics page's answer. The GPU
 environment is now decided first; when there is one and the entry has an
 Exec line, the application is started through the forking or systemd
 runner instead of Activate. Without a GPU environment it is activated as
 before. Tests: shouldStartAnActivatableApplicationOnItsGpu, an entry in
 Elisa's form with and without a GPU to run on.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed, edition-only (builds on the Graphics page patch before it)
Last-Update: 2026-10-24

